      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "# Input Adapter\n\nGodot object ( Gd<GR3DInputAdapter> )\nInterface GR3D uses to assemble a HashMap of input key/value pairs that this peer should send over the\nnetwork\n\n- all_inputs: Array<String>\n\n#[func(virtual)]\nfn get_input( input_key: String ) -> Variant:\n    Must return something for all possible input_keys that your game will ask for\n    e.g.\n\n    match input_key:\n        \"move\":\n            return Input.get_vector(\"move_left\", \"move_right\", \"move_forward\", \"move_backward\")\n        \"jump\":\n            return Input.is_action_just_pressed(\"jump\")\n        _:\n            push_error(\"Unknown input_key: \", input_key)\n\n--- private\n\nfn get_inputs() -> HashMap<input_key: String, input_value: Variant>:\n    iterate over all_input_keys and call get_input(input_key), which returns a Variant (I think ??)\n    append each Variant value into the returned hashmap\n\nfn get_ser_inputs() -> Vec<u8>:\n    hashmap = get_all_inputs\n    sort the hashmap alphabetically by input_key\n    push each value in the sorted hashmap into a Vec<Variant>\n    serialize the Vec<Variant> -> Vec<u8>\n\nfn deserialize_inputs(&self, ser_inputs: Vec<u8>) -> HashMap<input_key: String, input_value: Variant>:\n    let sorted = alphabetically sorted version of all_inputs\n    iterate over ser_inputs\n    insert_key = sorted[index]\n    value_type = \n    insert key from all_inputs = \n\n    index corresponds to ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "# Input Adapter\n\nGodot object ( Gd<GR3DInputAdapter> )\nInterface GR3D uses to assemble a HashMap of input key/value pairs that this peer should send over the network\n\n- all_inputs: Array<String>\n\n#[func(virtual)]\nfn get_input( input_key: String ) -> Variant:\n    Must return something for all possible input_keys that your game will ask for\n    e.g.\n\n    match input_key:\n        \"move\":\n            return Input.get_vector(\"move_left\", \"move_right\", \"move_forward\", \"move_backward\")\n        \"jump\":\n            return Input.is_action_just_pressed(\"jump\")\n        _:\n            push_error(\"Unknown input_key: \", input_key)\n\n--- private\n\nfn get_inputs() -> HashMap<input_key: String, input_value: Variant>:\n    iterate over all_input_keys and call get_input(input_key), which returns a Variant (I think ??)\n    append each Variant value into the returned hashmap\n\nfn get_ser_inputs() -> Vec<u8>:\n    hashmap = get_all_inputs\n    sort the hashmap alphabetically by input_key\n    push each value in the sorted hashmap into a Vec<Variant>\n    serialize the Vec<Variant> -> Vec<u8>\n\nfn deserialize_inputs(&self, ser_inputs: Vec<u8>) -> HashMap<input_key: String, input_value: Variant>:\n    let sorted = alphabetically sorted version of all_inputs\n    iterate over ser_inputs\n    insert_key = sorted[index]\n    value_type = \n    insert key from all_inputs = \n\n    index corresponds to ",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
